# Security rules

Use `@.cursor/reference/security-boundary.md` as the trust model.

- Keep `nodeIntegration: false`, `contextIsolation: true`, sandbox, web
  security, restrictive CSP, and navigation/window/permission blocking.
- Allowlist channels, verify the sender, and Zod-parse values before storage or
  file access.
- Never accept renderer-controlled SQL, table/column names, channels, absolute
  paths, shell commands, or generic filesystem operations.
- Resolve paths against their allowed root and reject traversal/symlinks.
- Attachments are JPG/JPEG/PNG/PDF, at most 25 MB, copied to generated internal
  names and opened only by explicit user action.
- Restore rejects absolute/traversal/symlink/unexpected/duplicate ZIP entries,
  incompatible manifests, and excessive extraction. Validate staging fully
  before a safety backup and live-data swap.
- UI errors and committed logs never expose restaurant records, invoice
  contents, attachment data, backup contents, stacks, SQL, secrets, or
  unintended local paths.
- Any new network, external URL, file format, shell, native dependency, or
  privilege requires an explicit threat review and negative tests.
